Z||000000||JetroGT||11-19-1999||05:10 AM||||<BR>Since Spring I think I've dumped over three thousand into my 86 SE. First was the engine. Revalved heads along with two new exhaust manifolds, throttle, intake, alternator, and electricial. Then the rack and pinion. One good tan cover for the drivers seat. Door skins with pockets. 120 Mph speedo. GT steering wheel. Subsystem, power mirrors and a starter.  And now the exhaust is done. It's new from the down pipe to the tips. All this and I'm still not done! <BR>Rear brakes and wheel berrings are next. I'm starting to get that droan in the car at certian speeds. I just hope a wheel dosen't fall off before I get a chance to fix it. If I ever get some pictures scanned I'll post them. Basically It's a black 86 SE with a messed up front cover. It started out as just a work car untill I could save for what I really want. An 88 GT with T-tops!<BR>||||reg||1
